# Pillow Thief mobile app environment (copy to .env — never commit real values)
# ==========================================
# This app is designed to run in Expo Go. It uses Expo Router for navigation,
# Supabase for backend (auth, bookings, payments), and react-native-maps for Google Maps.
#
# When running locally in Expo Go, the following must be set:
#   - EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL: Your Supabase project URL (e.g., https://your-project.supabase.co)
#   - EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY: Your Supabase anon key (generated from Supabase dashboard)
#
# Google Maps API keys are NOT required for Expo Go mode. The app is configured
# for sandbox mode (sandboxMode=true) which disables live map rendering and uses
# simulated maps. Set EXPO_PUBLIC_SANDBOX_MODE=true (already set) to enable this.
#
# To switch to production (live maps), set EXPO_PUBLIC_SANDBOX_MODE=false and provide valid
# Google Maps API keys in the app.json (see below).
#
# Required for local development:
#   - EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL (mandatory)
#   - EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY (mandatory)
#
# Example setup for Expo Go:
#   1. Create a Supabase project and get the URL + anon key
#   2. Copy this .env.example to .env in apps/mobile/
#   3. Fill in the two required lines above
#   4. Run: cd apps/mobile && npm install && npx expo start
#   5. Open Expo Go and scan the QR code (or enter exp://<your-lan-ip>:8081)
# ==========================================

# Supabase project (local dev: values from `supabase start`)
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Google Maps is configured natively via app.json (react-native-maps plugin)
# and requires a development build — it does NOT work in Expo Go.
# See docs/GOOGLE_MAPS.md for key creation + restriction steps.

# Set to "true" to show simulated-payment banners in dev only.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SANDBOX_MODE=true

# Optional: Enable debug logging for Google Maps (only in sandbox mode)
# EXPO_PUBLIC_DEBUG_LOGGING=false
